The commits in this repository are NOT signed. `git log --format='%G?'` returns `N` for every commit in this repository: there is no verifiable signature and none is claimed. A commit author's name is not a
signature, and the SHA-256 fingerprint a receipt carries is a digest without a key — it proves the
receipt was not edited after it was written, and it proves nothing about who wrote it.

Andrés Peña Mellado built this repository with a local Git configuration under the name
"Muse Sparks <muse-sparks@vespi.local>" and confirmed it on 2026-09-27, so the license has a single
holder and could be relicensed. The history is not rewritten: the tags and the receipts that point
at these commits must keep pointing at them. The agreed mechanism is a `.mailmap` joining
"Muse Sparks" to andresanemic; GitHub does not read `.mailmap`, so the older commits keep showing
as "Muse Sparks" in the web interface either way.
